import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Commutator.Basic
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.FinitelyPresentedGroup
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Finiteness
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Simple

/-!
# The Boone–Higman conjecture for finitely presented metabelian groups

J. Belk, C. Bleak, F. Matucci and M. C. B. Zaremsky, *Progress around the
Boone–Higman conjecture*, arXiv:2306.16356v3 (22 May 2025), page 1, state the
conjecture of Boone and Higman, verbatim:

> A finitely generated group G has solvable word problem if and only if it
> embeds into some finitely presented simple group.

Their Problem 5.3, on page 17, asks, verbatim:

> Problem 5.3. Prove the Boone–Higman conjecture for:
> …
> (7) Finitely presented metabelian groups.

Footnote 9 on the same page recalls that every finitely generated metabelian
group embeds into a finitely presented one (Baumslag and Remeslennikov) and that
such groups have solvable word problem (Baumslag).  One direction of the
conjecture holds for every finitely generated group (Kuznetsov; the survey's
Proposition 3.1).  So for this class the content of item (7) is the embedding,
which is the form in which the survey's own Theorem 5.1 records the solved
cases: "The following groups embed into finitely presented simple groups".

The two theorems below state that embedding:

* `finitely_presented_metabelian_embeds_in_finitely_presented_simple` is item
  (7): every finitely presented metabelian group embeds in a finitely presented
  simple group;
* `finitely_generated_metabelian_embeds_in_finitely_presented_simple` is the
  same for every finitely generated metabelian group.  It implies the first,
  since a finitely presented group is finitely generated, and by footnote 9 the
  two are equivalent.

## Vocabulary

Everything except the two definitions of the shared block is Mathlib's:
`Group.IsFinitelyPresented` is finite presentability (a surjection from a free
group of finite rank whose kernel is finitely normally generated), `Group.FG` is
finite generation, `IsSimpleGroup` is simplicity (the group is nontrivial and
every normal subgroup is `⊥` or `⊤`), `commutator G` is the derived subgroup
`G' = ⁅G, G⁆`, and `⁅H, K⁆` is the subgroup generated by the commutators of
elements of `H` and `K`.

* `IsMetabelianGroup G` says that the derived subgroup is abelian, that is, the
  second derived subgroup `⁅G', G'⁆` is trivial and the derived length is at most
  two.  Abelian groups count as metabelian.
* `EmbedsInFinitelyPresentedSimpleGroup G` says that some finitely presented
  simple group `S` receives an injective homomorphism from `G`.

All groups are quantified over `Type`.

## Scope, mismatches and limitations

* The conjecture is a biconditional about solvability of the word problem.  The
  theorems state only the embedding, for every group of the class and with no
  word-problem hypothesis, which is the direction Problem 5.3 asks for; the other
  direction is Kuznetsov's observation and is not formalized here.
* The permitted axioms are `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.
* The repository is released under Apache-2.0; the production process, AI
  involvement and the absence of human expert review are recorded in
  `README.md`.

The prose of this module was written by Claude (Anthropic).
-/

namespace MetabelianBooneHigman

-- BEGIN SHARED BLOCK (kept byte-identical in `Palomar/MetabelianBooneHigmanChallenge.lean` and `Palomar/MetabelianBooneHigmanSolution.lean`)

/-- A group is metabelian when its derived subgroup `G' = ⁅G, G⁆` is abelian, that
is, when the second derived subgroup `⁅G', G'⁆` is trivial. -/
def IsMetabelianGroup (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ⁅commutator G, commutator G⁆ = ⊥

/-- `G` embeds into some finitely presented simple group: the target of the
Boone–Higman conjecture (Belk–Bleak–Matucci–Zaremsky, arXiv:2306.16356v3,
page 1). -/
def EmbedsInFinitelyPresentedSimpleGroup (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ (S : Type) (_ : Group S), Group.IsFinitelyPresented S ∧ IsSimpleGroup S ∧
    ∃ f : G →* S, Function.Injective f

-- END SHARED BLOCK

/-- **Item (7) of Problem 5.3 of Belk–Bleak–Matucci–Zaremsky**: every finitely
presented metabelian group embeds in a finitely presented simple group. -/
theorem finitely_presented_metabelian_embeds_in_finitely_presented_simple :
    ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], Group.IsFinitelyPresented G → IsMetabelianGroup G →
      EmbedsInFinitelyPresentedSimpleGroup G := by
  sorry

/-- **The finitely generated form**: every finitely generated metabelian group
embeds in a finitely presented simple group. -/
theorem finitely_generated_metabelian_embeds_in_finitely_presented_simple :
    ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], Group.FG G → IsMetabelianGroup G →
      EmbedsInFinitelyPresentedSimpleGroup G := by
  sorry

end MetabelianBooneHigman
